      "details": "Implement a comprehensive WhatsApp integration module using Evolution API REST endpoints. Create a new inbox provider class inheriting from Chatwoot's base inbox structure. Set up API client for Evolution API communication with proper authentication and error handling. Implement instance creation functionality using Baileys through POST /instance/create endpoint with custom instance names. Build QR code generation and display interface by calling GET /instance/connect/{instanceName} and rendering the base64 QR code image in the frontend. Implement SMS code verification as alternative connection method using POST /instance/code endpoint. Create connection status monitoring using GET /instance/connectionState/{instanceName} with real-time updates via WebSocket or polling. Add webhook configuration for receiving messages using POST /webhook/set endpoint pointing to Chatwoot's webhook handler. Implement message sending capabilities using POST /message/sendText and POST /message/sendMedia endpoints. Create inbox configuration UI allowing users to set custom names, choose connection methods (QR/SMS), and monitor connection status. Add proper error handling for API failures, connection timeouts, and instance management issues. Ensure proper cleanup of disconnected instances and implement reconnection logic. Store Evolution API credentials and instance configurations securely in encrypted application credentials.",
      "testStrategy": "Create comprehensive test suite including unit tests for Evolution API client methods, integration tests for instance creation and connection flows, and end-to-end tests for complete WhatsApp inbox setup. Test QR code generation and display functionality with mock Evolution API responses. Verify SMS verification flow with test phone numbers. Test message sending and receiving through webhook endpoints using ngrok for local development. Validate connection status monitoring with simulated connection state changes. Test error handling scenarios including API timeouts, invalid credentials, and network failures. Perform load testing with multiple concurrent WhatsApp instances. Verify proper cleanup of disconnected instances and test reconnection scenarios. Test inbox configuration UI across different browsers and screen sizes. Validate webhook security and message processing accuracy.",
